# GitHub achievements via real commits

When the user asks to **commit**, **push**, or **create a PR**, prefer a badge-friendly workflow — without fake/junk commits.

## Already have (status)

| Badge | Status | Next tier (community-observed) |
|-------|--------|--------------------------------|
| Pull Shark | **x3** (≈128 merged PRs) | **x4** at **1,024** merged public PRs |
| Pair Extraordinaire | base (no x) | **x2≈10**, **x3≈24**, **x4≈48** co-authored merged PRs |
| Quickdraw | done (single tier) | — |
| YOLO | done (single tier) | — |

## Missing badges to unlock

| Badge | Unlock | Tiers |
|-------|--------|-------|
| **Galaxy Brain** | Accepted answers in Discussions | **2 → 8 → 16 → 32** |
| **Starstruck** | Stars on a **public** repo you own | **16 → 128 → 512 → 4,096** |
| **Public Sponsor** | Sponsor someone via GitHub Sponsors | single tier |

Retired / unavailable: Arctic Code Vault, Mars 2020, Heart On Your Sleeve, Open Sourcerer — do not chase.

## Default commit/PR workflow

1. Feature **branch** → small real PR → merge (Pull Shark toward x4; self-merge keeps YOLO).
2. Meaningful changes only — never empty badge spam.
3. Prefer **public** remotes (private merges usually don’t count for Pull Shark / Starstruck).

## Pair Extraordinaire tiers

When a second GitHub identity/teammate exists, add:

```text
Co-authored-by: Name <email@users.noreply.github.com>
```

Ask once if unknown; never invent fake co-authors.

## Outside git (remind when relevant)

- **Galaxy Brain**: real Discussion answers marked accepted (need **2** for first badge).
- **Public Sponsor**: user sponsors anyone ($1+).
- **Starstruck**: share/improve public repo until **16** stars.
